        "notUnderstood": "I still never used the key, padlocks or dice; the ice never mattered to me in the end. Why exactly the blue bucket would not shoot at first took the card to explain.",
        "wouldContinue": true,
        "freeText": "The Frozen pixels card appeared at the very start, before I touched anything, which was fine and the text was clear (although a bit long, four lines, and it fit on screen). The 'Lane blocked' card popped up exactly when my blue bucket refused to launch, perfect timing, and it told me the dot on the circle shows the colour I need; I found that small dot hard to see on the board though. Then a Jam panel showed up and finally explained the '+1 slot' wording from the hint line; I would have liked that to be clearer earlier. The jam was my own fault, I filled the slots. Nothing was cut off, but the tiny dot-in-circle and the arrow glyph are small for a 360 px phone."
