        "freeText": "The Stones card was readable and its picture (paint -> stone -> blocked pixel) made sense, but it came late for me. Columns with three buckets: I did not see a '+N' label under any column on this level, so I could not check that card. The top hints ('Relaunch first the waiting one with no arrow', 'All come back: if it jams, use +1 slot') are readable, but the arrow glyph inside quotation marks is tiny on a 360 px screen and I only half understood the ones about ' +1 slot' until I jammed. I jammed again because the lane-blocked yellow had to be launched with both slots full; that felt slightly unfair because the game would not let me launch the thing that was blocking, without filling slots first. Took many moves (18), a bit long but fun."
